{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_nxidmurwbowxvetaw4a5zozekpoqfpehgpo7k77gql4zesje73dq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_bdrk_01Wjro9QtieA3nYLceGJ7J7U","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/local/home/scheschb/.harvest/work/harvest-work-lpPs9a/translation/ERRORS.md","old_string":"## Notes on faithfulness\n\n* E7 and E24 are genuine memory-safety faults in the C.  The differential tests\n  execute both libraries in a **forked child** and compare the *termination\n  signal*, so \"C segfaults ⇒ Rust segfaults too\" is asserted rather than\n  glossed over.  The Rust translation reproduces E24 with\n  `ptr::read_volatile(modes.as_ptr().offset(mode_index as isize))` — the same\n  out-of-bounds stack read — and E7 by calling libc `strcmp` directly.","new_string":"## Notes on faithfulness\n\n* E7 is a genuine, *deterministic* memory-safety fault: `strcmp(NULL, …)` always\n  faults.  The differential test executes both libraries in a **forked child**\n  and compares the *termination signal*, so \"C segfaults ⇒ Rust segfaults with\n  the same signal\" is asserted rather than glossed over.\n* E11–E18: Rust's `as` operator **saturates**, which would diverge from\n  `cvttsd2si`.  The translation therefore routes every `double`→`int` conversion\n  through `d2i()`, which returns `INT_MIN` for NaN/∞/out-of-range, matching\n  x86-64 gcc bit-for-bit.\n\n### E24 is not a contract — measured evidence\n\n`modes` is a four-element array of `const char *` in `modeselect`'s own stack\nframe.  A negative `mode_index` reads the bytes *below* it, which are whatever\nthe previous use of that stack region left behind.  Measured with\n`libharvest-work-lpPs9a.so` (the very same `.so`, the very same argument\n`modeselect(-3, 1, 1, 1)`):\n\n| caller context | C library outcome |\n|---|---|\n| fresh process, called from `main` (standalone driver) | `SIGSEGV` |\n| forked child of the test harness, stack left as-is | returns `112527`, prints a garbage mode name and `(0x0)` |\n| forked child, 32 KiB of stack below pre-filled with `0x00…` | `SIGSEGV` |\n| forked child, 32 KiB of stack below pre-filled with `&\"turbo\"` | returns `113295`, prints `Selected mode: turbo (0x30)` |\n\nThe result therefore is **not a function of the arguments**, so no translation\n(in Rust or in C) can be required to reproduce it byte-for-byte.  The Rust\ntranslation performs the *structurally identical* operation —\n`ptr::read_volatile(modes.as_ptr().offset(mode_index as isize))` on its own\n4-element stack array, with `read_volatile` so the optimiser may not exploit the\nUB — and the differential test asserts everything that *is* well defined:\n\n1. with the stack region deterministically zeroed, the OOB read yields `NULL` in\n   both libraries and both die with the *same* signal (`SIGSEGV`);\n2. every value the garbage read could possibly produce for `mode_value`\n   (`0x00`, `0x10`, `0x20`, `0x30`, `0x40`) is fed through the rest of the\n   pipeline via the low-level exports of both libraries, and the two must agree\n   exactly — i.e. the whole negative-index code path is verified apart from the\n   one unspecified load;\n3. if the garbage happens to be a readable string in one library but not the\n   other, the test still checks that whichever run completed satisfies the\n   `mode_value`-parameterised formula from (2)."}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":116682,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":558,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":21,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cc07b24-a1a6-4436-bcd1-d9e9880595e3","uuid":"484ba600-7007-42f9-a6a9-5a7bd852f688","timestamp":"2026-08-28T04:34:23.493Z"}
