{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_cfxf3a7ad2d54yhiiwkkackvewzfkcjeoerpk7q4sw4jccvmwtoq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification is complete. All four phases pass across every configuration.\n\n## What I did\n\n**Phase A — artifacts** (`translation/SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md`, `CONFIGS.md`), derived mechanically from `c_src/src/lib.c`:\n- 7 exported symbols, all present in both `.so`s; no untranslated module.\n- **30 error rows** — the library has no error convention at all, so I enumerated the two fallback sentinels (`0x00`, `0xDEAD`), every UB-dependent result (`double`→`int` casts, signed overflow, signed shift overflow), and the two reachable hard faults.\n- **69 configuration rows** across all 7 entry points, including the six low-level ones `modeselect` composes.\n\n**Phases B/C/D — tests** in `translation/tests/`: both libraries loaded via `libloading` and called only through their exported C symbols. `modeselect`'s 8 `printf` calls are compared **byte-for-byte** by redirecting fd 1; genuine fault paths run in a forked child so the *termination signal* is compared, not just \"both failed\".\n\n**Result: 103 tests × 3 feature combos × 2 profiles = 618 passes, 0 failures.** Symbol diff empty in both profiles.\n\n## Three findings worth your attention\n\n1. **`cargo test` does not relink a `cdylib`.** I hit this for real: a mutation-test leftover (`0xBEEF`→`0xBEEE`) survived in `target/debug/libmodeselect_lib.so` while `src/lib.rs` was already correct — a green suite against a stale artifact. I added a mtime staleness guard in `tests/common/mod.rs` that refuses to run, and `run_verification.sh` always does an explicit `cargo build --lib --examples` first.\n\n2. **`time(NULL)` hid an entire axis.** `current >> 29` is the constant `3` until 2038, so arithmetic vs *logical* shift was indistinguishable — a mutant survived. I added an `LD_PRELOAD` `time()` interposer (`examples/faketime.rs`) and re-run the suite under 25 forced clocks including negatives and `i64::MIN/MAX`. Both shift mutants are now caught, and this added rows C64–C69.\n\n3. **ERRORS.md row E24 is not a testable contract, and I corrected my own initial assumption.** My first E24 test asserted \"both must SIGSEGV\" and failed. Investigating showed the negative-index read of `modes[-1..-3]` is uninitialized stack, so the *same C `.so` with the same argument* yields either `SIGSEGV` or `113295` depending only on caller stack content (measured four ways, documented in ERRORS.md). I replaced the bogus assertion with three tests covering what *is* defined: identical faults under a deterministically zeroed stack, agreement across every `mode_value` the garbage load could produce, and a formula check on any run that completes.\n\n## Anti-vacuity evidence\n\nI mutation-tested the suite: **22 of 24 single-edit mutants detected**. The two survivors are provably equivalent (`result1`/`result2` are only ever `0` or `INT_MIN`, so `&0xFF` vs `&0x1FF` and `&0xFF00` vs `&0xFFFF` are identical) — documented rather than papered over.\n\nI made no changes to `c_src/` (only the required `build/` output) and no changes to `src/lib.rs` — the translation was already correct; the defects were in my harness and artifacts. Re-run everything with `cd translation && ./run_verification.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":761,"cache_read_input_tokens":198527,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":761,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5cc07b24-a1a6-4436-bcd1-d9e9880595e3","uuid":"0c17e36c-ffa9-4e88-8d6f-0f0e7038fcee","timestamp":"2026-08-28T04:57:34.287Z"}
